task_prompts.click-deb1f0e1:
When a prompt has confirmation_prompt=True and default="" (empty string), entering an empty string should be accepted as the value, but currently it seems to be rejected or mishandled, forcing a non-empty confirmation to match. For example:

```python
import click

@click.command()
@click.option("--password", prompt=True, hide_input=True, default="", confirmation_prompt=True)
def cli(password):
    click.echo(password)

cli(input="\n")
```

Entering nothing (empty string) for both the prompt and confirmation should succeed and return "", matching the given default. Please fix prompt() so empty string input is accepted when confirmation_prompt=True and default="".

